 "reconciliation": "NINETEEN of the twenty columns stated here close exactly, residual zero on every one; ONE does not, and one of the nineteen closes only by construction. Both are recorded rather than forced. FIRST, f_10_15: the footing glyph sits under the closing rule and is not settled, so its printed total is null and the read 8 stands unchecked; the cells of lines 23 and 24 that make up five of that 8 are written as two and three separate strokes rather than as formed numerals, and the enumerator elsewhere on this leaf writes 2 as a formed numeral (line 26 of the male 20-under-30 column). SECOND, m_20_30 closes on 33 only because lines 20 and 27 are read AS 3 each from that footing; their glyph is not the form this hand uses for 3 at line 8, and it is the form the footing's own second digit uses. Both readings are inferences from the footing, are labelled as such on the column, and are not independent corroboration of it. THE FREE COLOURED BLOCK IS NOT EMPTY on this leaf: its footing row carries exactly one figure, a 1 in males 55 under 100, and the one written mark in that block stands at line 13 - a household with NO free white cell at all, whose head is therefore enumerated as a free coloured man.",
